# SPA deep-link fallback for the static demos (Cloudflare Pages).
#
# The demos (participant-portal, application-admin-console) are client-routed SPAs
# staged under /portal-demo/ and /admin-demo/. Reloading a client route such as
# /portal-demo/problems/x has no matching file; a 200 rewrite serves each SPA's own
# index.html (its assets are absolute, /portal-demo/..., so they resolve) while
# keeping the URL for the router. Cloudflare serves existing files first, so real
# assets under these prefixes are unaffected; only non-existent (client-route)
# paths hit the rewrite.
#
# In practice these rewrites have NOT been reliable in production: without a
# 404.html Cloudflare enters implicit SPA mode and serves the ROOT index.html for
# unknown paths, which takes precedence over these rules (community-reported
# behavior). Two repo-side layers make demo deep links survive regardless:
#   1. landing/404.html exists — this disables implicit SPA mode, so unknown
#      paths get a real 404 instead of the unstyled landing.
#   2. Both landing/index.html and landing/404.html carry a head-top recovery
#      script: if either page is served under /portal-demo/ or /admin-demo/,
#      it immediately redirects to that SPA's real index with the original
#      route in ?goto=<path>, and RootEntryPage restores the route client-side.
/portal-demo/*  /portal-demo/index.html  200
/admin-demo/*   /admin-demo/index.html   200
